  <VME_CultOfPersonalityDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: story(priority=-999)->-->
    <li>story(priority=-999)-&gt;</li>
    <!--EN: setup->There is no order without a firm hand directing things. This was clear to [founderName], our first [leaderTitle].-->
    <li>setup-&gt;没有坚定的意志就没有秩序。这一点对[founderName]，我们的第一位[leaderTitle]来说非常清楚。</li>
    <!--EN: setup->We are the Chosen of [founder_possessive] Divine Will. The sons and daughters of [founderName] [honorific], our first [leaderTitle].-->
    <li>setup-&gt;我们是神的旨意[founder_possessive]的选民。[founderName][honorific]的子女，是我们第一任[leaderTitle]。</li>
    <!--EN: setup->It is told that the first [leaderTitle] of our people, [founderName] [honorific] was forged by the Universe from the clay of creation itself.-->
    <li>setup-&gt;据说我们人类的第一位[leaderTitle]，[founderName][honorific]是宇宙之主以创世之土铸造的。</li>
    <!--EN: setup->From the terrible chaos embraced by our ancients arose [founderName], our first [leaderTitle].-->
    <li>setup-&gt;从我们祖先可怕而混沌的拥抱中诞生了[founderName]，我们的第一任[leaderTitle]。</li>
    <!--EN: setup->From humble and unremarkable origins, [founderName], our first [leaderTitle], raised above [founder_possessive] station, imposing [founder_possessive] unwavering will.-->
    <li>setup-&gt;[founderName]，我们的第一位领袖[leaderTitle]，来自于卑微而平庸的凡世，超越了[founder_possessive]的地位，树立起[founder_possessive]的坚定意志。</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Magnificent-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;壮丽的</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Great-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;伟大的</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Saint-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;神圣的</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Awe-Inspiring-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;令人敬畏的</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Conqueror-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;征服者</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Resplendent-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;辉煌的</li>
    <!--EN: story(uses=1,priority=-10)->The [memberNamePlural] swore eternal loyalty to [founderName] and [founder_possessive] descendants, forever bound in devoted servitude.-->
    <li>story(uses=1,priority=-10)-&gt;[memberNamePlural]宣誓永远效忠[founderName]和[founder_possessive]的后代，愿永远被束缚在忠诚的奴役中。</li>
    <!--EN: story(uses=1,priority=-10)->[founderName] inspired many to lead a life of righteousness, and thus received our unnending devotion.-->
    <li>story(uses=1,priority=-10)-&gt;[founderName]激励着许多人向往正直的生活，并因此得到我们无尽的奉献。</li>
    <!--EN: story(uses=1,priority=-10)->With an army of [founder_possessive] followers at [founder_possessive] command, the line of [founderName] has lasted till the present, represented by our beloved leader.-->
    <li>story(uses=1,priority=-10)-&gt;有一群[founder_possessive]的追随者在[founder_possessive]的领导下，我们敬爱的领袖[founderName]，这一家族得以延续至今。</li>
    <!--EN: story(uses=1,priority=-10)->Our beloved leader, the latest successor of [founderName], will bring us to prosperity, allowing all of us to live a [memeAdjective] life.-->
    <li>story(uses=1,priority=-10)-&gt;我们敬爱的领袖，[founderName]的最新继任者，将为我们带来繁荣，让我们每个人都过上[memeAdjective]的生活。</li>
  </VME_CultOfPersonalityDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_EschatologismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: eschatologismBasis   ->This world is tainted, impure, and it must be purged. We shall bring the end of days and a new Universe will be reborn from the ashes of the current one.-->
    <li>eschatologismBasis   -&gt;这个世界是肮脏的，不纯洁的，它必须被净化。我们将为其带来末日，一个新的宇宙将从当前宇宙的灰烬中涅槃重生。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismBasis   ->There is nothing of value in this world anymore. Vast post-human intelligences scheming in the dark. Vicious genetically engineered creations rampaging across the land. Greedy, stupid, ambitious humans preying on the weak. It must all be destroyed.-->
    <li>eschatologismBasis   -&gt;这世上已经没有什么值得存在的东西了。巨大的人工智能在黑暗中谋划着阴谋，邪恶的基因工程创造物在大地上横冲直撞。贪婪，愚蠢，野心勃勃的人类只会掠夺弱者。这些必须全部毁灭。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismBasis   ->This world needs to be purged. Too long have we left it go unchecked. Human stupidity running rampant and ruining everything.-->
    <li>eschatologismBasis   -&gt;这个世界需要净化，我们放任自流太久了。人类愚蠢横行，毁灭了一切。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismBasis   ->It is an inescapable fact: the only way forward is to start over and begin anew. This world must be destroyed.-->
    <li>eschatologismBasis   -&gt;这是一个不可避免的事实：前进的唯一途径便是重生。让我们重新开始，这个旧世界必须毁灭。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismBasis   ->There is no longer room for compromise. This world is tainted, impure. It must be destroyed.-->
    <li>eschatologismBasis   -&gt;再也没有妥协的余地了。这个世界是如此肮脏而不纯洁，它必须被摧毁。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismFact    ->Either through atomic fire or another means, we must bring the Apocalypse.-->
    <li>eschatologismFact    -&gt;不管是通过核能、烈焰，还是其他方式，我们都必须为旧世界带来天启。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismFact    ->The Great Battle at the End of Everything is coming, and we will be prepared.-->
    <li>eschatologismFact    -&gt;最后的伟大战役即将来临，我们必须做好准备。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismFact    ->No one must be left alive to rebuild, for the seeds of corruption lie deep within each and any of us.-->
    <li>eschatologismFact    -&gt;不能让任何人活到重建之日，因为腐败的种子会深埋在我们每个人的内心深处。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismFact    ->Nothing but charred remains should be left.-->
    <li>eschatologismFact    -&gt;除了烧焦的残骸什么都不会留下。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismFact    ->Once everything has been destroyed. We, the Chosen, shall recreate the world to our liking.-->
    <li>eschatologismFact    -&gt;一旦一切都被摧毁。我们作为天选之子，将按照我们的规划重建这个世界。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismProphecy->We will be triumphant.-->
    <li>eschatologismProphecy-&gt;我们将会胜利。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismProphecy->No one shall be ready for our wrath.-->
    <li>eschatologismProphecy-&gt;没人能承受我们的愤怒。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismProphecy->When we finally strike, all shall fall before us.-->
    <li>eschatologismProphecy-&gt;当最终我们出击时，所有人都会倒在我们面前。</li>
    <!--EN: eschatologismProphecy->The days of this world are counted.-->
    <li>eschatologismProphecy-&gt;世界末日即将来临。</li>
  </VME_EschatologismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_EsotericismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: esotericismBasis   ->Beyond the grasp of common science, there is an unsurpassed wealth of secret knowledge.-->
    <li>esotericismBasis   -&gt;在普通科学的范畴之外，还有大量禁忌的神秘学知识。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismBasis   ->Hidden to the prying eyes of scientists and philosophers, an occult world of hidden knowledge awaits.-->
    <li>esotericismBasis   -&gt;在科学家和哲学家的窥视下，一个隐藏着知识的神秘世界在等待着你。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismBasis   ->Science can only bring you so far. Beyond the veil of reality there is a trove of secret knowledge, waiting to be uncovered.-->
    <li>esotericismBasis   -&gt;科学只能给你带来这么多。在现实的面纱之外，有大量的神秘学知识等待着被发现。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismBasis   ->The Universe is too vast to be limited to the constraints of pure math and physics. Beyond such human limitations there is a vast treasure of secret knowledge that can be accessed by those willing to do so at any cost necessary.-->
    <li>esotericismBasis   -&gt;宇宙如此浩瀚，绝不会仅仅单纯受限于数学和物理。在这些人类的认知之外，有一个巨大的神秘学知识宝库，可以由那些愿意不惜任何代价探索的人所获取。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismFact    ->Only a select few have the mental strength to acquire such insights.-->
    <li>esotericismFact    -&gt;只有少数精挑细选出来的人才有获得这种洞察力的精神力量。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismFact    ->These occult insights are not for everyone. Only a small group of sages can explore and observe them. The Chosen Ones.-->
    <li>esotericismFact    -&gt;这些神秘的见解并不适合所有人。只有一小群圣贤才能观察和探索它们。做出选择吧。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismFact    ->Such insights would probably be too much for the common folk. Only those with great mental fortitude can peer into the occult... and keep their minds intact.-->
    <li>esotericismFact    -&gt;对于普通人来说，这样的见解可能难以被接受。只有那些意志坚强的人才能窥探到神秘的事物并保持他们的心智完整。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismProphecy->Perhaps by delving into such knowledge we can even trascend our mortal existence.-->
    <li>esotericismProphecy-&gt;也许通过钻研这些知识，我们甚至可以追溯到让我们终有一死的存在。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismProphecy->Given enough time, we will crack the most guarded secrets, and finally understand our place in this Universe.-->
    <li>esotericismProphecy-&gt;只要有足够的时间，我们就能破解这些严加保守的秘密，最终了解我们在宇宙中的位置。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismProphecy->The alchemists of antiquity might not have been so foolish in their search for gold, but we are much more ambitious: we will apply the transmundane to our very souls and become more than human.-->
    <li>esotericismProphecy-&gt;古代的炼金术士在寻找黄金时可能不会如此愚蠢，但我们要更加雄心勃勃：我们要把超凡的东西应用到我们的灵魂之中，使自己超越人类。</li>
    <!--EN: esotericismProphecy->With such knowledge, we will have a clear advantage over the rest of this planet's inhabitants, and our domination will be all but secured.-->
    <li>esotericismProphecy-&gt;有了这样的知识，我们将比这个星球上的其他居民有更加明显的优势，我们的统治几乎不会遭受任何威胁。</li>
  </VME_EsotericismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_HedonistDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: lesson(priority=-1)->stuff happens-->
    <li>lesson(priority=-1)-&gt;事情发生</li>
    <!--EN: r_pattern->"[r_lessonIntro] [r_lessonMain]. [r_lessonReinforcement]"\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]-->
    <li>r_pattern-&gt;"[r_lessonIntro][r_lessonMain]。[r_lessonReinforcement]"\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution(p=2)-><i>[attributionSource_titleCase]</i> by [founder_nameFull]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution(p=2)-&gt;</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]'s letter to [believer_nameFull]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]给[believer_nameFull]的信</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], on [founder_possessive] deathbed-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]，在[founder_possessive]临终之前。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], just before execution-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]，就在执行之前</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], [speech] on the [TerrainFeature]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[TerrainFeature]上的[founder_nameFull]，[speech]</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], [speech] in the [Community]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[Community]中的[founder_nameFull]，[speech]</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->[memeConcept]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[memeConcept]</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->[memeAdjective] [memeConcept]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[memeAdjective][memeConcept]</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->A [memeAdjective] Life-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[memeAdjective]的生活</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->Reflections by a [attributionJob]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[attributionJob]的反映</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->Journal of a [attributionJob]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[attributionJob]的日志</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->Thoughts of a [attributionJob]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[attributionJob]的想法</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->Life of a [attributionJob]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[attributionJob]的生活</li>
    <!--EN: attributionJob->[memeAdjective] [place_job]-->
    <li>attributionJob-&gt;[memeAdjective][place_job]</li>
    <!--EN: attributionJob->[place_job]-->
    <li>attributionJob-&gt;[place_job]</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Speech-->
    <li>speech-&gt;Speech</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Address-->
    <li>speech-&gt;Address</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->After so many sleepless nights of careful deliberation, I came to a simple conclussion:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;经过这么多不眠之夜的深思熟虑，我得出了一个简单的结论:</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->What is a fundamental truth of human existence?-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;人类存在的基本真理是什么?</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->I have suffered a lot in this life. But this suffering has taught me a simple principle:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我这一生经历了很多苦难。但这些痛苦教授了我一个简单的原则</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Growing in squalor on the [place_summary] [place_name], I learned a sincere axiom:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;在[place_summary][place_name]的肮脏环境中成长，我学会了一个真理:</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Internalize this lesson, for it will serve you well:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;将这一课内化，因为它会很好地帮助你:</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Are you feeling lost? Perhaps you haven't yet figured out this very simple concept:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;你感到迷茫吗?也许你还没有弄明白这个简单的概念:</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->They tried to tempt me with a life of rich, dull productivity, but they couldn't fool me:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;他们试图用一种物质丰富而精神匮乏的多产生活来诱惑我，但他们无法愚弄我:</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->pleasure, the satisfaction of bodily desires, is the highest good and proper aim of human life. Whether through religion or philosophy our entire lives should be focused on enjoying ourselves as much as possible-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;愉悦，即肉体欲望的满足，是人类生活的最高善与正当目标。无论是通过宗教还是哲学，我们的整个生活都应该专注于尽可能地自我享受</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->I finally figured out the only reason to be alive is to enjoy it-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;我终于明白了活着的唯一理由，那就是享受生活</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->the only way to get rid of temptation is to yield to it-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;摆脱诱惑的唯一方法就是屈服于诱惑</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->salvation is for the feeble. I don't want salvation, I want life, all of life, the miserable as well as the superb-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;拯救是为软弱的人。我不需要拯救，我需要的是生命，所有的生命，无论是悲惨的还是卓越的</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->pleasure is not a need, but an incentive-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;快乐不是一种需求，而是一种激励</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->the most responsible way of life right now is to enjoy ourselves while we can-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;现在最负责任的生活方式是在我们可以享受的时候不忘享受生活</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->you can live to be a hundred if you give up all the things that make you want to live to be a hundred-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;如果你放弃所有让你想活到100岁的念想，你就可以活到100岁</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->No one can argue with that.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;没有人能反驳这一点。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Only fools think otherwise.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;只有傻瓜才不这么想。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->And as we now know, that was soon to become evident to everyone.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;正如我们现在所知道的，这一点很快就显而易见了。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Everything that has happened since has reinforced that fact.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;此后发生的一切都强调了这一事实。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->It is as if that is etched directly into my mind.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;这句话似乎已经深深地印在我的脑海里了。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->It is something I'll never forget.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;这是我永远不会忘记的事情。</li>
  </VME_HedonistDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_OmnismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: episode(priority=-1)->-->
    <li>episode(priority=-1)-&gt;</li>
    <!--EN: creation->It is limiting beyond words to bind oneself to any particular god or belief. The combined gifts of all supreme beings, philosophers and forces is what should truly be appreciated.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;把自己束缚在任何特定的神或信仰上是难以言表的。所有至高无上的生命、哲学和力量的结合才是真正值得我们欣赏的。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->All religions and ideologies point to the whole truth, that a single transcendent purpose unites all things.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;所有的宗教和意识形态全部都指向真理，那就是一个单一的、超然的目的，它会将所有的事物联合起来。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->It seems that the teachings of the ancient [religion] and [religion2] scholars had a lot of truth to teach us.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;看来古代[religion]和[religion2]的学者有许多真理要传授给我们。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->Truth can be found in all religions and ideologies, as they are all part of the greater human experience. Whether it is the teachings of the [religion] texts or the philosophies of the ancient [religion2] scholars, we can learn about the universe by opening our minds to this truth.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;真理可以在所有的宗教和意识形态中找到，因为它们都是人类实践的一部分。无论是[religion]文献的教导还是[religion2]学者的哲学理念，我们都可以通过开放我们的思想理念来了解这些真理，来了解真实的宇宙。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->Human beings are inquisitive creatures, and as such we have invented some incredible concepts: either [religion] teachings or [religion2] tennets hold a portion of the complete truth, and as such all beliefs are intrinsically true and useful.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;人类是充满好奇的生物，因此我们发明了一些不可思议的理念：无论是[religion]的教义还是[religion2]的信条中都含有一定的真理，从而可见任何信仰本质上都是有可取之处的。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->All religions and ideologies are legitimate. A single transcendent purpose unites all things and people, and you can reach this universal purpose by any means, either by the study of the ancient [religion] texts or by following the [religion2] dogma.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;任何宗教与意识形态都是合法的。一个单一的、超然的目标将所有的事物和人联系起来，你可以通过任何手段来达成这个目标，要么通过研究古代[religion]的文献，要么遵循[religion2]的教义。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->Only through carefully studying all beliefs can we truly understand the nature of reality.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;只有通过仔细研究所有的信仰，我们才能真正理解真理的本质。</li>
