  <VME_PantheismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: episode(priority=-1)->-->
    <li>episode(priority=-1)-&gt;</li>
    <!--EN: creation->[deity0_name] is in all things. We are all made from stardust, and we are a part of divinity as much as any [Animal] might be.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;[deity0_name]存在于万物之中。我们都是由星尘组成的，我们和任何[Animal]一样都是神性的一部分。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->Everything is part of an all-encompassing, immanent God, [deity0_name]. All forms of reality may then be considered either modes of that Being, or identical with it.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;一切都是无所不包的、上帝[deity0_name]内在的一部分。一切形式的实在，可以认为是存在的形式，或与存在相同。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->The Universe, in the sense of the totality of all existence, and God are identical. Divinity is all around us, forming [deity0_name].-->
    <li>creation-&gt;就所有存在的整体而言，宇宙和上帝是完全等同的。神性就在我们周围，形成了[deity0_name]。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->There was a neverending void. In that void, [deity0_name] was formed, thus beginning the reckoning of time.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;有一片永无止尽的虚空。在那片虚空中，[deity0_name]形成了，于是开始了时间的计算。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->Only through carefully studying [deity0_name] can we truly understand the nature of reality.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;只有通过仔细研究[deity0_name]，我们才能真正理解实相的本质。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->We must recognize this immanent divinity in everything around us, and respect all creations inside [deity0_name] as sacred.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;我们必须认识到我们周围一切事物内在的神性，并尊重所有内在的创造物[deity0_name]是神圣的。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->If we want to truly understand the nature of [deity0_name] we must engage in quiet and respectful contemplation of everything on it.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;如果我们想真正了解神[deity0_name]的本质，我们必须安静地、恭敬地执行上面的一切。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->Controlling [deity0_name] would be a natural consequence of our own intrinsic divinity.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;控制[deity0_name]将是我们自身内在神性的自然结果。</li>
  </VME_PantheismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_SecularSpiritualityDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: lesson(priority=-1)->stuff happens-->
    <li>lesson(priority=-1)-&gt;事情发生</li>
    <!--EN: r_pattern->"[r_lessonIntro] [r_lesson]. [r_lessonReinforcement]"\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]-->
    <li>r_pattern-&gt;"[r_lessonIntro] [r_lesson]。[r_lessonReinforcement]"\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]'s letter to [believer_nameFull]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]给[believer_nameFull]的信</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], on [founder_possessive] mindfulness dissertation-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]，关于[founder_possessive]的</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], [speech] on the [TerrainFeature]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull], [speech]在[TerrainFeature]</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], [speech] in the [Community]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull], [speech]在[Community]</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Meditation Speech-->
    <li>speech-&gt;冥想演讲</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Know-Yourself Address-->
    <li>speech-&gt;了解你自己的所在</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->I always repeat, "letting go is the hardest asana":-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我总是重复，“放手是最难的形式”:</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->It took me long years of intense meditation to understand that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我花了很多年的时间才明白这一点</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->We must not be like the [foeLeader], who don't know themselves. Observing them did teach me one thing:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我们不能像[foeLeader]那样，连自己都无法认知。观察他们确实教会了我一件事</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->By teaching Yoga on the [place_summary] [place_name], I realized that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;通过在[place_summary][place_name]上传授瑜伽，我意识到</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Find your center and set intentions for the day as you begin to focus on your breath – body connection. You will then realize that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;当你开始专注于你的呼吸与身体的协调时，找到你的重心并为这一天设定目标。然后你就会意识到</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->You must start with a series of breath to movement flows, energizing and invigorating the body and the mind. And you will finally know that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;你必须从一系列的呼吸到最细微的动作开始，使心灵和肉体充满精神与活力。你最终会明白的</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->A flower does not think of competing to the flower next to it. It just blooms. One thing will become increasingly clear then: that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;一朵花没必要与它旁边的花竞争，它只是花朵而已。到那时，有一件事将变得越来越清楚:那就是</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->You will begin the journey of the self, through the self, to the self. Then you'll see that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;你将开始一段自我之旅，通过自我，抵达自我。然后你会看到</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->You cannot always control what goes on outside. But you can always control what goes on inside. Once that is achieved you will see that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;虽然你不能控制外在发生的事，但你可以控制自己内在的事。一旦实现这些，你就会明白</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->The longest journey of any person is the journey inward. This journey shows you that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;每个人人生中最漫长的旅程就是内心的旅程。这场旅行向你展示了这一点</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Truth lies in pursuing a spiritual philosophy without adherence to a religion, personal growth and inner peace of an individual are more important than a relationship with the divine, and thus-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;真理在于追求一种精神哲学而不是恪守宗教，个人的成长和内心的平静比与神的关系更为重要，因此</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Just breathe.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;简单的深呼吸就好。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Be where you are, not where you think you should be.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;到你现在所在的地方，而不是你认为应该去的地方。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->The pose begins when you want to leave it.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;当你想离开的时候，这个构成就开始了。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Inhale the future, exhale the past.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;吸入未来，呼出过去。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->It's not about being good at something. It's about being good to yourself.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;这不是关于是否擅长某件事，而是对自己要求更好一点。</li>
  </VME_SecularSpiritualityDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_SerketistDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->There is no higher lifeform than the Hive Queens. Their nourishing jelly is like ambrosia, and the entire world should be remade in their image.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;没有比蜂巢女王更高等的生命形式了。它们的滋养虫胶就像美味佳肴，整个世界都应该按照它们的形象重塑。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->In its hubris, humanity accidentally stumbled upon the creation of the perfect lifeform: Insectoids.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;在它的傲慢中，人类意外地发现了完美的生命形式:虫群。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->The runaway creation of some forgotten ancient geneticist, Insectoids have evolved to become the perfect lifeform.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;一些被人遗忘的由古代遗传学家创造的失控虫族已经进化成完美的生命形式。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->Threatened by the Mechanoid menace, mankind engineered the perfect lifeform: Insectoids.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;由于受到机械族的威胁，人类创造了完美的生命形式:虫族。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->Led by the sacred Hive Queens, Insectoids are the perfect lifeform in the galaxy.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;在神圣的虫巢女王带领下，虫族是银河系中最完美的生命形式。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistFact    ->They are the pinnacle of evolution. [InsectAdjective]. [InsectAdjective2]. [InsectAdjective3]. Everyone should strive to become like them.-->
    <li>serketistFact    -&gt;它们是进化的巅峰。[InsectAdjective]，[InsectAdjective2]，[InsectAdjective3]，每个人都应该努力成为它们那样的人。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistProphecy->[itIsSaid] we will learn from them, becoming like a tidal wave that will wash over our enemies.-->
    <li>serketistProphecy-&gt;[itIsSaid]我们将向它们学习，像潮水一样席卷我们的敌人。</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->Perhaps, with time,-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;也许,随着时间的推移,</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->It is written in our destiny that-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;我们的命运注定</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->Either through technology or more arcane means-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;要么通过科技，要么通过更加神秘的手段</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->We will revere their ways, their collective intelligence and-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;我们将尊重它们的行为和它们的集体智慧</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->By revering the Will of the Hive Queen-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;通过尊重虫群女王的意志</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective->Adaptive-->
    <li>InsectAdjective-&gt;自适应</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective->Ravenous-->
    <li>InsectAdjective-&gt;贪婪的</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective->Overpowering-->
    <li>InsectAdjective-&gt;压倒性的</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective2->Versatile-->
    <li>InsectAdjective2-&gt;多才多艺的</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective2->Uncompromising-->
    <li>InsectAdjective2-&gt;坚定的</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective2->Destructive-->
    <li>InsectAdjective2-&gt;毁灭性的</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective3->Complex-->
    <li>InsectAdjective3-&gt;复杂的</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective3->Indestructible-->
    <li>InsectAdjective3-&gt;不可毁灭的</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective3->Resistant-->
    <li>InsectAdjective3-&gt;反抗的</li>
  </VME_SerketistDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_TaoismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: episode(priority=-1)->-->
    <li>episode(priority=-1)-&gt;</li>
    <!--EN: r_pattern->"[r_creation] [r_episode] [r_episode]."\n\n  - Lao Tzu, Tao Te Ching-->
    <li>r_pattern-&gt;"[r_creation] [r_episode] [r_episode]"\n\n  - 老子，《道德经》</li>
    <!--EN: creation->By living in harmony with the Tao, one can achieve perfection and become one with the unplanned rhythms of the universe.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;道生一，一生二，二生三，三生万物。万物负阴而抱阳，冲气以为和。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->Being deeply loved by someone gives you strength, while loving someone deeply gives you courage.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;人爱者有力 爱人者勇。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->Simplicity, patience, compassion. These three are the greatest treasures.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;我有三宝,持而保之,一曰慈、二曰俭、三曰不敢为天下先。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->The journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;千里之行，始于足下。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->Life is a series of natural and spontaneous changes. Don't resist them; that only creates sorrow. Let reality be reality. Let things flow naturally forward in whatever way they like.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;人法地，地法天，天法道，道法自然。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->When you are content to be simply yourself and don't compare or compete, everyone will respect you.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;甘美食，美其服，安其居，乐其俗。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->The truth is not always beautiful, nor beautiful words the truth.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;信言不美，美言不信。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->Because one believes in oneself, one doesn't try to convince others. Because one is content with oneself, one doesn't need others' approval. Because one accepts oneself, the whole world accepts him or her.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;果而勿矜，果而勿伐，果而勿骄，果而不得已，果而勿强。物壮则老，是谓不道，不道早已。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->Care about what other people think and you will always be their prisoner.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;富贵而骄，自遗其咎。</li>
  </VME_TaoismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
